ues what does my analysis suggests  for the direction of this country for  the guiding assumptions for our grand  strategy I would really pass along three  pieces of advice to the people who are  running the country mile or two down the  road and they would be the following one  that America was a general boon to the  world for the last 50 years in part  because we got our internationalism  right we worked through institutions we  were not predatory we did not beat our  chest and run around and tell other  countries what to do and that's because  we told the American people that we  needed institution centrism to work with  others and what I fear is happening  today is that nobody is out there trying  to rebuild that internationalism that  moderate center in this country I don't  see any politician who is really making  that a top priority and I think if you  look at our universities we're not  teaching history if students don't know  about World War two they don't know what  happened in this world then how are we  ever going to get our internationalism  right how we're going to keep this  country on a steady course in the world  so I think a national priority ought to  beat education leadership on the  question of how this country wheels its  power second rather than practicing a  kind of foisting ourselves and in others  leading with this notion of preeminence  I think we should do exactly the  opposite and practice strategic  restraint and compromise a country that  is this powerful risks losing its most  precious commodity commodity which is  its legitimacy the sense abroad that we  are a benign power and not a predatory  power we are in the midst of losing that  if we lose that then a country this  strong is going to scare the rest of the  world and push them away from us that's  exactly what again these pupils are  showing we ought to do what Britain did  to us in the late 19th century see that  we are emerging  make room for others so rather than  trying to b